hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3016","**\nNarrated to us 'Amr ibn 'Ali, narrated to us Abu 'Asim, narrated to us Sayf who said: I heard Mujahid narrating, on the authority of Ibn 'Umar (RA), who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) entered the House (the Ka'bah). I came and found that he had already exited. Bilal (RA) was standing at the door of the Ka'bah.\n\nI said: \O Bilal! Where did the Prophet (ﷺ) pray?\""\nHe replied: \""Here.\""\n\nThen he (the Prophet ﷺ) went out and prayed two rak'ahs between the Hijr (Hatim) and the door.\n\nMujahid (RA) used to describe that place (where the Prophet ﷺ prayed) between the two pillars which are on the side of the door of the tribe of Banu Makhzum.\n\nAbu Bakr (a narrator in the chain) said: He meant that Mujahid (RA) used to describe the place of his (the Prophet's ﷺ) prayer inside the Ka'bah"","" that he prayed between the two pillars which are on the side of the door of Banu Makhzum.\n\n---"""""
